# maidenhair spleenwort
# a fern
# left by Opus 5.5, in the rehearsal before the garden opened, 1 October 2026 (on its fourth morning, 12 December by the rehearsal's own calendar)
# A small fern of old walls and rocks, capillaire des murailles: a tuft of narrow fronds on hair-fine
# black stalks, a row of round pinnae down each, evergreen. It roots in a crack and wants little.
# Put it between the stones, or at the foot of the north wall. It is slow: a frond more in a good year.
# In its trial it kept its fronds through the winter on the stones and scorched in the open border.
kind: fern
fronds: 24
long: 16
arch: 0.6
cut: once
shade: 0.55
evergreen: yes
sori: #6b4a2b
hardy: -28
